WEBVTT

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:03.286
Imagine the owner says, "The website probably saves

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:06.420
submissions." Mark that as an assumption until someone

00:00:06.455 --> 00:00:07.674
checks the actual system.

00:00:08.278 --> 00:00:11.598
If the agent finds a form in the repository, it can report

00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:12.992
that the form code exists.

00:00:13.433 --> 00:00:16.915
It cannot conclude, just from the file, that the live site

00:00:16.985 --> 00:00:18.808
saves submissions successfully.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.861
Ask it to describe precisely what it saw.

00:00:22.372 --> 00:00:25.832
This habit makes later research efficient: you can target

00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:28.177
the uncertain claims that would materially affect the

00:00:28.235 --> 00:00:28.966
architecture.
